    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0264" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.6363/7–648</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Diplomatic Representatives in
                        the American Republics </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-06">July 6, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State encloses for the Mission’s information a copy of a
                        report<anchor n="1" xml:id="d192-f1"/> of the investigation of petroleum in
                    relation to national defense conducted by the Special Subcommittee on Petroleum,
                    Committee of the Armed Services, House of Representatives, usually known as the
                    “Dewey Short Committee”.</p>
                <pb facs="0265" n="249" xml:id="pg249"/>
                <p>The report contains much valuable information relating to the oil industry and
                    pertinent to the Department’s responsibilities in this field, and it is
                    recommended that it be read by all officers whose work deals with petroleum.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
